request:
one put, with the peer traffic behind it duplicated and reordered

m1 POST /v3/kv/put  write s53/k0 once, while a quarter of peer messages are duplicated
    {"key":"czUzL2sw","value":"b25jZQ=="}
m2 POST /v3/kv/range  m2's copy: version tells whether the write was applied more than once
    {"key":"czUzL2sw"}
m3 POST /v3/kv/range  m3's copy, which must match m2's exactly
    {"key":"czUzL2sw"}

response:
version 1 on every member, and create_revision equal to mod_revision

m1 200 OK
    {"header":{"cluster_id":"7322369447726496003","member_id":"3392855371301142761","revision":"2","raft_term":"2"}}
